    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d538">

                <pb facs="0700" n="580" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg580"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Griscom to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1905-03-13"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 13, 1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 201.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s No. 84 of
                    November 4, and to my No. 167 of January 12, 1905, in regard to the destruction
                    of sea fowl on the Midway and other American islands, I have the honor to
                    transmit inclosed herewith a copy of a translation of a note received on the
                    21st ultimo from the minister of foreign affairs, giving further assurances of
                    the efforts of the Japanese Government to stop these depredations.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lloyd Griscom.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d538-a1.xml" xpointer="d538-a1"/>
